# Chat Module Width

The chat module's **load default** depends on the **size of the display**, not the size of the browser window. The user can still cycle single → double → fill → custom in-session; the next load reapplies this default (do not restore the last toggle). Triple is not a rest state.

## Breakpoint

**1512 CSS pixels** — the 14" MacBook Pro class, measured with **`window.screen.width`**.

- **≤ 1512** → default **single** (tier 0, `--chat-pane-w` / 380px)
- **> 1512** → default **double** (tier 1, typically 580px)

Source of truth: `WPaneWidth.defaultChatTier()` in `js/pane-width.js` (FOUC twin in `js/text-size-fouc.js` as `wiseDefaultChatTier`). Both call the one measurer, `window.WISE_CHAT_SCREEN_WIDTH_PX()`.

## Never measure `window.innerWidth` for this

`innerWidth` is the **viewport**. It changes when the window is resized, opened un-maximised, or has devtools docked — so on one physical screen the chat flipped between single and double for no reason the user could see. The tier must be a property of the screen, so that a given machine always opens the chat the same way.

`innerWidth` survives only as the fallback inside `screenWidthPx()`, for a browser that will not report `screen.width` at all.

## Re-applying on a display change

Moving the window to a different monitor is the only thing that can legitimately change the tier. `js/text-size-fouc.js` watches for it and re-applies — but skips when `html[data-chat-width-user-set="1"]` is set, so a manual in-session toggle is never stomped. `js/pane-width.js` sets that flag from one delegated capture-phase click listener covering every module's width control; individual toggle handlers do not need to set it.

## The control always changes the width

Tapping the width button **must move the module every time**, whether or not anything is docked beside it. On `wiseai.html` it did not: the welcome chat fills the row, and every rule that could size it sat behind `#modules-row:has(.wa-pane.is-open)`, so with no output open the classes, the icon and the caption all advanced while the module stayed the full width of the row.

Two pieces keep it live, and a new host needs both:

- **The host sizes the module once the member owns its width.** `.wa-chat[data-width-user-set]` carries the same tier widths as the docked rules, so load is untouched — a fresh page still opens with the chat filling the row at its screen default — and the first tap pins it for real. `js/wiseai-chat.js` sets that attribute (via `WPaneWidth.markModuleUserSet`) rather than relying on the capture listener, which only fires for trusted clicks.
- **A free-growing module is not at the tier its classes claim.** The chat's toggle measures `flex-grow` and, on the first tap only, enters the cycle at its first preset instead of advancing. Without this, single → double → fill all resolve to "the whole row" and the member taps once or twice before anything moves.

Custom is the one stop that keeps the width you arrived with. That is its documented behaviour app-wide, not a dead tap.

`scripts/_chat_width_probe.py` drives the whole cycle with and without an output pane open, at both screen defaults, and prints the measured width after every tap.

## Rules for the agent

- Never hard-reset a chat to `wide: 0` / `widthTier = 0` on load. Use `defaultChatTier()`. A `: 0` fallback on the end of a `wiseDefaultChatTier` check is the same bug — it silently pins the chat to single on any page where load order puts the module first.
- Apply the default through the existing `panel-wide` / `panel-triple` / `panel-fill` classes and the width-toggle button. Do not invent a parallel width system.
- When the user cycles back to single, drop `html.chat-default-double` so the FOUC class cannot pin the chat wide.
- Right-of-chat modules still default to **fill** (`js/default-fill.js`). That rule is unchanged.
- **Chat still does not restore a session choice.** `#agent-main` and every other non-chat module persist their own rest state per page (`wise-module-width-tiers-v1`), keyed by the module, so changing or resizing a neighbour cannot write this one. Do not revive the old shared keys (`wise-main-width` / `wise-all-modules-width`) that pinned every page to one width.
- On `wiseai.html`, the welcome chat still fills the row **on load**. Never gate the tier widths on a pane being open — see "The control always changes the width" above.
